# AI Development Protocol

Apply this protocol when the request may modify software code, behavior, tests, technical configuration, schemas, dependencies, build/deployment mechanics, or CC Flow itself. Before editing, read `AGENTS.md`, `.ai/project.md`, `.ai/profile.md`, `.ai/architecture.md`, `.ai/business.md`, `.ai/conventions.md`, and `.ai/progress.md`.

For read-only questions, explanations, exploration, research, reports, summaries, status checks, or standalone document creation, do not create or update CC Flow records unless explicitly requested.

Use an active task under `.ai/tasks/` for non-simple work. Follow the stage gates in `.ai/conventions.md`, keep changes within scope, record actual verification commands, update affected documentation, and never claim unrun tests passed.
